red_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T09:22:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T09:22:59Z","body":"There is no made issue about the bug I just found a bug and fixes it myself instead of making an issue ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765094840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765201754","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114824#issuecomment-3765201754","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114824","id":3765201754,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gbGta","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T11:40:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T11:41:59Z","body":"> There is no made issue about the bug I just found a bug and fixes it myself instead of making an issue\r\n\r\nNext time when you find a bug, it's better to post an issue first and then make an pr and link to it. In the issue you can describe the problem in detail so it will make more sense to everyone who have the same problem as you","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765201754/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765207693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114824#issuecomment-3765207693","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114824","id":3765207693,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gbIKN","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T11:48:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T11:48:40Z","body":"I don't think that's a correct fix, you're basically making the camera smoothing ignore the time scale. I think it makes sense that e.g. `2.0` time scale would make the smoothing happen twice as fast.\r\n\r\nBut the issue is: the current implementation for the Camera2D smoothing is buggy.\r\n- It's delta time dependent (e.g. 2 frames with `0.1` delta will result in different smoothed position than 1 frame with `0.2` delta).\r\n- It can overshoot the target ([when `position_smoothing_speed * delta > 1.0`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9/scene/2d/camera_2d.cpp#L199-L200)).\r\n- [The smoothing is potentially done multiple times per frame](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9/scene/2d/camera_2d.cpp#L191-L195).\r\n- (maybe more issues)\r\n\r\nI think for 4.6 we should probably go only for a simple fix (4.6 is in Release-Candidate stage) instead of reimplementing it properly, as this might change the behavior too much? Not sure. 🤔 Anyway, a simple fix would be to ensure there's no target overshooting (that's what likely happens [in the video](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114824#issue-3799555896)). So changing this line:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9/scene/2d/camera_2d.cpp#L199\r\nlike:\r\n```\r\nreal_t c = MIN(1.0f, position_smoothing_speed * delta); \r\n```\r\n\r\nPlease try testing such solution. This I think would be safe to include in `4.6`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> There is no made issue about the bug I just found a bug and fixes it myself instead of making an issue\r\n\r\nReporting a bug and explaining the details there + providing reproduction project is still welcomed, unless it's trivial to reproduce. Here you have to have at least some movement code for the camera (or whatever the camera is attached to), which can vary, so I'd say providing a reproduction project makes sense. If not opening a bug report, then at least providing such repro project in here ([in the PR description](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114824#issue-3799555896)).\r\nNevertheless, of course thanks for trying to fix this! 🙂","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765207693/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765270862","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114824#issuecomment-3765270862","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114824","id":3765270862,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gbXlO","user":{"login":"totoriel","id":132148700,"node_id":"U_kgDOB-Bt3A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132148700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel","html_url":"https://github.com/totoriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T13:05:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T13:05:28Z","body":"> I don't think that's a correct fix, you're basically making the camera smoothing ignore the time scale. I think it makes sense that e.g. `2.0` time scale would make the smoothing happen twice as fast.\r\n> \r\n> But the issue is: the current implementation for the Camera2D smoothing is buggy.\r\n> \r\n> * It's delta time dependent (e.g. 2 frames with `0.1` delta will result in different smoothed position than 1 frame with `0.2` delta).\r\n> * It can overshoot the target ([when `position_smoothing_speed * delta > 1.0`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9/scene/2d/camera_2d.cpp#L199-L200)).\r\n> * [The smoothing is potentially done multiple times per frame](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9/scene/2d/camera_2d.cpp#L191-L195).\r\n> * (maybe more issues)\r\n> \r\n> I think for 4.6 we should probably go only for a simple fix (4.6 is in Release-Candidate stage) instead of reimplementing it properly, as this might change the behavior too much? Not sure. 🤔 Anyway, a simple fix would be to ensure there's no target overshooting (that's what likely happens [in the video](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114824#issue-3799555896)). So changing this line:\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9/scene/2d/camera_2d.cpp#L199\r\n> \r\n> \r\n> like:\r\n> ```\r\n> real_t c = MIN(1.0f, position_smoothing_speed * delta); \r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Please try testing such solution. This I think would be safe to include in `4.6`.\r\n> \r\n> > There is no made issue about the bug I just found a bug and fixes it myself instead of making an issue\r\n> \r\n> Reporting a bug and explaining the details there + providing reproduction project is still welcomed, unless it's trivial to reproduce. Here you have to have at least some movement code for the camera (or whatever the camera is attached to), which can vary, so I'd say providing a reproduction project makes sense. If not opening a bug report, then at least providing such repro project in here ([in the PR description](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114824#issue-3799555896)). Nevertheless, of course thanks for trying to fix this! 🙂\r\n\r\nI just tried it, and yes, it is a good idea. It did work, but can you create an issue for the camera problems you mentioned above so I can work on reworking it for 4.7?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765270862/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3801426363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114824#issuecomment-3801426363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114824","id":3801426363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ilSm7","user":{"login":"ettiSurreal","id":98223724,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdrGbA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98223724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal","html_url":"https://github.com/ettiSurreal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type"